<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Talbot, 1st Earl of Shrewsbury</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1387–<a href="/years/1453">1453</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as John Talbot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Talbot, 1st Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a>, was an English soldier and the most famous English commander of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. Captured at Patay in 1429 and created Earl of Shrewsbury in 1442, he fought for decades in Normandy and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In 1452 he led an army to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> at the citizens' invitation, and he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-castillon">Battle of Castillon</a> in July 1453.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-talbot-1st-earl-of-shrewsbury.jpg" alt="John Talbot, 1st Earl of Shrewsbury" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poems and Romances (Shrewsbury book), illuminated by the MASTER OF JOHN TALBOT · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shrewsbury_Book_f.2_(Talbot-Dog).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
